course: dictionary
lesson: 8510
title: Satellite
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A satellite is a machine that people send into space, or a natural object that travels around a planet. «A satnav or phone finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites in orbit.» Here the satellites are machines sent up into space, and orbit is the path they travel around the Earth.
explain: The Moon is Earth's natural satellite, because it travels around our planet without anyone building it. «A satellite in orbit is falling around the Earth while it moves sideways very fast.» That clue tells you why satellites keep going round instead of crashing down.
explain: Look at the words near satellite to find its job. «Beavers build dams of sticks, stones and mud... and shows up in satellite pictures.» Satellite comes before pictures, so it tells you how the pictures were taken: from a satellite high above the Earth. Ask yourself: what does the word next to it describe?
fact: A satellite is a machine sent into space to travel around the Earth or another planet.
fact: The Moon is a natural satellite: it travels around Earth and nobody built it.
fact: Satellites are used for communication, weather forecasts, maps and science.
fact: «Satellite» before a noun means using satellites, as in satellite TV or satellite pictures.
fact: Satellites stay in orbit because they are falling around the Earth while moving sideways very fast.
exercise: «A satnav or phone finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites in orbit.» What are the satellites here? | Clouds that bring rain | Small rocks that fall to the ground | *Machines sent into space that travel around the Earth | Roads for cars
exercise: The Moon is Earth's natural satellite. Why is the Moon called a natural satellite? | *It is a natural object that travels around the Earth | It is a machine that sends signals to phones | It is a shop in space | It was built by people in a factory
exercise: «Satellite pictures» show a place from above. What does satellite tell you about these pictures? | *They were taken using a satellite in space | They show only the sea | They are very old paintings | They are only black and white
test: «Live bus stop signs use the GPS position each bus sends, worked out from satellites in space.» What are the satellites doing in this sentence? | Stopping the buses on the road | *Helping to work out where each bus is | Cleaning the bus stop signs | Cooking the driver's lunch
test: In «satellite TV», satellite is used before a noun. What does it mean? | A small moon going around a planet | Lost somewhere in space | A kind of cloud that brings rain | *Using satellites to send TV pictures and sound
exam: Which of these is Earth's natural satellite? | A weather machine sent up by scientists | *The Moon | A satellite dish on a roof | A satnav in a car
